{
  "title": "Saga – Orchestration",
  "level": "container",
  "layout": {
    "primaryFlow": "book"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "traveller",
      "type": "person",
      "label": "Traveller",
      "description": "Books a flight and a hotel in one go."
    },
    {
      "id": "trips",
      "type": "api",
      "label": "Trips API",
      "technology": "Go",
      "description": "Takes a trip request and starts its booking workflow."
    },
    {
      "id": "orchestrator",
      "type": "service",
      "label": "Booking Orchestrator",
      "technology": "Temporal",
      "replicas": 2,
      "description": "Runs each step in turn and undoes the done ones on failure.",
      "inside": {
        "level": "component",
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "o.trips",
            "type": "api",
            "label": "Trips API",
            "technology": "Go"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.workflow",
            "type": "component",
            "label": "BookTrip Workflow",
            "technology": "Temporal",
            "description": "Runs the steps; keeps the undo stack."
          },
          {
            "id": "o.flights",
            "type": "adapter",
            "label": "Flight Activities",
            "description": "Holds and releases seats."
          },
          {
            "id": "o.hotels",
            "type": "adapter",
            "label": "Hotel Activities",
            "description": "Reserves and cancels rooms."
          },
          {
            "id": "o.payments",
            "type": "adapter",
            "label": "Payment Activities",
            "description": "Charges the trip."
          },
          {
            "id": "o.flights-svc",
            "type": "api",
            "label": "Flights Service",
            "technology": "Spring Boot 3"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.hotels-svc",
            "type": "api",
            "label": "Hotels Service",
            "technology": "Kotlin"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.payments-svc",
            "type": "api",
            "label": "Payments Service",
            "technology": "Go"
          }
        ],
        "relationships": [
          {
            "id": "o.start",
            "from": "o.trips",
            "to": "o.workflow",
            "label": "StartWorkflow",
            "semantic": "command"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.hold",
            "from": "o.workflow",
            "to": "o.flights",
            "label": "holdSeat()",
            "semantic": "uses"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.reserve",
            "from": "o.workflow",
            "to": "o.hotels",
            "label": "reserveRoom()",
            "semantic": "uses"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.charge",
            "from": "o.workflow",
            "to": "o.payments",
            "label": "charge()",
            "semantic": "uses"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.flights-call",
            "from": "o.flights",
            "to": "o.flights-svc",
            "label": "POST /holds",
            "semantic": "http"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.hotels-call",
            "from": "o.hotels",
            "to": "o.hotels-svc",
            "label": "POST /reservations",
            "semantic": "http"
          },
          {
            "id": "o.payments-call",
            "from": "o.payments",
            "to": "o.payments-svc",
            "label": "POST /charges",
            "semantic": "http"
          }
        ],
        "flows": [
          {
            "id": "o.flow",
            "title": "Book a trip, inside the orchestrator",
            "color": "blue",
            "steps": [
              {
                "relationship": "o.start",
                "caption": "Temporal records the start; the workflow survives any worker restart."
              },
              {
                "relationship": "o.hold",
                "caption": "Each step is an activity: retried on its own, its result kept in history."
              },
              "o.flights-call",
              {
                "relationship": "o.reserve",
                "caption": "A done step pushes its compensation onto the stack."
              },
              "o.hotels-call",
              {
                "relationship": "o.charge",
                "caption": "Last, and the riskiest: if it fails, the stack is unwound."
              },
              "o.payments-call"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "place": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 120
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "flights",
      "type": "api",
      "label": "Flights Service",
      "technology": "Spring Boot 3",
      "description": "Holds seats on a flight."
    },
    {
      "id": "flights-db",
      "type": "sql-database",
      "label": "Flights DB",
      "technology": "PostgreSQL 16",
      "description": "Seat holds and tickets."
    },
    {
      "id": "hotels",
      "type": "api",
      "label": "Hotels Service",
      "technology": "Kotlin",
      "description": "Reserves hotel rooms."
    },
    {
      "id": "hotels-db",
      "type": "nosql-database",
      "label": "Hotels DB",
      "technology": "MongoDB 7",
      "description": "Room reservations."
    },
    {
      "id": "payments",
      "type": "api",
      "label": "Payments Service",
      "technology": "Go",
      "description": "Charges the trip total."
    },
    {
      "id": "stripe",
      "type": "external-system",
      "label": "Stripe",
      "technology": "Stripe",
      "description": "Charges cards."
    }
  ],
  "relationships": [
    {
      "id": "request",
      "from": "traveller",
      "to": "trips",
      "label": "Books a trip"
    },
    {
      "id": "start",
      "from": "trips",
      "to": "orchestrator",
      "label": "Starts BookTrip",
      "semantic": "command"
    },
    {
      "id": "hold-seat",
      "from": "orchestrator",
      "to": "flights",
      "label": "POST /holds",
      "semantic": "http"
    },
    {
      "id": "reserve-room",
      "from": "orchestrator",
      "to": "hotels",
      "label": "POST /reservations",
      "semantic": "http"
    },
    {
      "id": "charge",
      "from": "orchestrator",
      "to": "payments",
      "label": "POST /charges",
      "semantic": "http"
    },
    {
      "id": "release-seat",
      "from": "orchestrator",
      "to": "flights",
      "label": "DELETE /holds/{id}",
      "semantic": "compensates",
      "compensationFor": "hold-seat",
      "compensationName": "Release seat",
      "compensationProtocol": "http"
    },
    {
      "id": "cancel-room",
      "from": "orchestrator",
      "to": "hotels",
      "label": "DELETE /reservations/{id}",
      "semantic": "compensates",
      "compensationFor": "reserve-room",
      "compensationName": "Cancel room",
      "compensationProtocol": "http"
    },
    {
      "id": "flights-tx",
      "from": "flights",
      "to": "flights-db",
      "semantic": "readsWrites"
    },
    {
      "id": "hotels-tx",
      "from": "hotels",
      "to": "hotels-db",
      "semantic": "readsWrites"
    },
    {
      "id": "card",
      "from": "payments",
      "to": "stripe",
      "label": "Charges card",
      "semantic": "http",
      "response": true
    }
  ],
  "flows": [
    {
      "id": "book",
      "title": "Book a trip",
      "color": "teal",
      "steps": [
        {
          "relationship": "request",
          "caption": "The traveller confirms a flight and a hotel together."
        },
        {
          "relationship": "start",
          "caption": "The API starts a BookTrip workflow and answers with its id."
        },
        {
          "relationship": "hold-seat",
          "caption": "Step 1: a seat is held, committed in the Flights DB alone.",
          "highlight": [
            "flights-tx"
          ]
        },
        {
          "relationship": "reserve-room",
          "caption": "Step 2 starts only once step 1 has answered.",
          "highlight": [
            "hotels-tx"
          ]
        },
        {
          "relationship": "charge",
          "caption": "Step 3, the riskiest last: the trip total is charged."
        },
        {
          "relationship": "card",
          "caption": "The card is accepted; the workflow completes and the trip is booked."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "declined",
      "title": "Card declined",
      "color": "rose",
      "variantOf": "book",
      "steps": [
        {
          "relationship": "charge",
          "caption": "The charge comes back 402: the card is declined."
        },
        {
          "relationship": "cancel-room",
          "caption": "The orchestrator undoes the last done step first: the room."
        },
        {
          "relationship": "release-seat",
          "caption": "Then the seat. The trip ends CANCELLED and the traveller is told."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "kind": "label",
      "attach": false,
      "text": "# Saga – Orchestration\nOne workflow books a trip, and undoes the finished steps when one fails.",
      "style": {
        "role": "title"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n.one",
      "kind": "decision",
      "about": "orchestrator",
      "text": "One place knows the trip's state: the orchestrator. Each service only knows its own step."
    },
    {
      "id": "n.wf",
      "kind": "code",
      "about": "orchestrator",
      "language": "plaintext",
      "code": "saga := NewCompensations()\nhold, err := HoldSeat(ctx, trip)\nif err != nil { return err }\nsaga.Add(ReleaseSeat, hold.ID)\n\nroom, err := ReserveRoom(ctx, trip)\nif err != nil { saga.Run(ctx); return err }\nsaga.Add(CancelRoom, room.ID)\n\nif err := Charge(ctx, trip); err != nil {\n  saga.Run(ctx) // newest first\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "n.idem",
      "kind": "warning",
      "about": "release-seat",
      "text": "Compensations are retried until they succeed, so every DELETE must be idempotent — releasing a seat twice is a no-op."
    },
    {
      "id": "n.semantic",
      "kind": "note",
      "about": "cancel-room",
      "text": "Not a rollback: the room was really reserved for a moment. A cancellation fee is a business decision, not a database one."
    }
  ],
  "_openPoints": [
    {
      "id": "op.timeout",
      "kind": "tentative",
      "context": "A hotel that does not answer in 30 s is treated as a failure, and the seat is released.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "kind": "edge",
          "id": "reserve-room"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sequences": [
    {
      "id": "seq",
      "title": "BookTrip, step by step",
      "mermaid": "sequenceDiagram\n  participant O as Booking Orchestrator\n  participant F as Flights Service\n  participant H as Hotels Service\n  participant P as Payments Service\n  O->>F: POST /holds\n  F-->>O: 201 Hold\n  O->>H: POST /reservations\n  H-->>O: 201 Reservation\n  O->>P: POST /charges\n  alt card accepted\n    P-->>O: 200 Charged\n  else card declined\n    P-->>O: 402 Declined\n    O->>H: DELETE /reservations/{id}\n    O->>F: DELETE /holds/{id}\n  end",
      "links": {
        "O": "orchestrator",
        "F": "flights",
        "H": "hotels",
        "P": "payments"
      }
    }
  ],
